# T7-LOCAL-NAMED-UNIT (steps/defects.md), a required positive, red: model's local S calls the unit method get, and model
# calls get itself; get reads node\cnt.  In the node w both run over the copy of the unit made at the merge, which
# holds 7; the root's poke writes the original's cnt 11 after.  S's get is selected through S's lexical links -- the
# copy's get -- as model's is: 7 * 10 + 7.  Native and root-walked code selects S's get in the program's unit
# (l2_m_unit_ref gives a method's own named Structure l2_program_unit): 11 * 10 + 7.  Exit 7; 81 otherwise.
int: cnt 7
fn: get () int
    return: node\cnt
fn: model (int: y) int
    S:
        int: v 0
        v: get()
    S
    return: S\v * 10 + get()
fn: wrap (int: k) fn: () int
    return: merge(y: k; model)
sub: poke ()
    node\cnt: 11
@: w wrap(5)
poke()
int: result w()
int: ok 7
if: result != 77
    ok: 81
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
